  view_file {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///public/assets/aistudio/Paste_October_25__2026_-_2_39PM_ecd881b2"
    end_line: 99
    content: "Build Bandobast \342\200\224 An Intelligent Event Operations Platform\r\n\r\nAct as a senior full-stack engineer, product designer, AI engineer and QA engineer. Build a polished, functional, production-minded web application called **Bandobast** for the PromptWars Challenge 5: Celebration & Event Planner.\r\n\r\nDo not stop after proposing a plan, generating wireframes or creating a landing page. Inspect the workspace, establish the architecture, implement the application, run it, test the critical workflows, fix errors and document how to use it.\r\n\r\nIf the workspace already contains a project, inspect it and preserve useful existing work. If it is empty, initialize the project. Work in manageable stages, but continue implementation without waiting for approval after each stage.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. PRODUCT VISION\r\n\r\n**Product:** Bandobast\r\n\r\n**Tagline:** One change. A thousand connections. Bandobast keeps it together.\r\n\r\n**Product description:** Bandobast is an AI-powered event operations platform that connects budgets, vendors, guest counts, family priorities and deadlines into one living plan. It helps event organizers understand how a change affects the entire event, compare meaningful alternatives and keep the plan synchronized.\r\n\r\n### Target persona\r\n\r\nInitially target the person coordinating a multi-function Indian wedding involving:\r\n\r\n- Mehendi\r\n- Sangeet\r\n- Wedding ceremony\r\n- Reception\r\n\r\nThey must manage a fixed budget, changing guest counts, vendor quotations, family preferences, bookings, deadlines and interconnected tasks.\r\n\r\nThe architecture should be reusable for engagements, birthdays and community festivals such as Navratri and Diwali, but the initial experience should focus on a multi-function Indian wedding.\r\n\r\n### The core differentiator\r\n\r\nDo not make this another generic AI chatbot or party-idea generator.\r\n\r\nBuild an event-management system that can:\r\n\r\n1. Understand the event and the organizer\'s constraints.\r\n2. Maintain a structured representation of the event.\r\n3. Calculate budgets and deadlines using deterministic code.\r\n4. Show how changes propagate through dependent tasks and costs.\r\n5. Generate alternative plans that respect the organizer\'s priorities.\r\n6. Extract and compare vendor quotations with clear source attribution.\r\n7. Apply an approved scenario to the actual event plan.\r\n\r\nThe application must be a responsive web application, not a native mobile app.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. VISUAL DESIGN SYSTEM \342\200\224 VERY IMPORTANT\r\n\r\nCreate a premium, warm, elegant and modern visual identity inspired by Indian celebrations.\r\n\r\n**Do not use dark blue, navy or purple as the main theme. Do not default to a generic dark SaaS dashboard.**\r\n\r\nUse this palette:\r\n\r\n- Warm ivory background: `#FAF7F0`\r\n- White/cream card surface: `#FFFDF9`\r\n- Forest olive: `#405B43`\r\n- Sage green: `#DCE6D6`\r\n- Marigold: `#E7A83E`\r\n- Terracotta: `#C76F50`\r\n- Espresso text: `#302F28`\r\n- Muted text: `#77756B`\r\n- Soft borders: `#E7E0D3`\r\n- Warning: a high-contrast amber treatment\r\n- Error: a clear, accessible red treatment\r\n\r\nUse forest olive for primary actions and selected navigation, marigold for celebration-related highlights and important metrics, terracotta for secondary accents, and sage for supportive panels and status indicators.\r\n\r\nMaintain readable contrast. Do not use pale text on pale backgrounds or rely on color alone to communicate a status.\r\n\r\n### Design language\r\n\r\n- Elegant editorial typography with a refined serif for major headings and a clean sans-serif for body text.\r\n- Use Playfair Display for selected display headings and Inter or a comparable sans-serif for interface text, with robust fallback fonts.\r\n- Generous whitespace, subtle borders, restrained shadows, rounded corners and clear visual hierarchy.\r\n- Use delicate geometric or floral motifs sparingly. Avoid excessive wedding clipart, gaudy gold gradients, stereotypical ethnic patterns or an overly decorative interface.\r\n- Use consistent Lucide icons.\r\n- Create a polished desktop dashboard with a fully usable mobile layout.\r\n- Add subtle transitions for navigation, cards, status changes and chart interactions.\r\n- Avoid excessive gradients, oversized hero sections inside the actual dashboard and unnecessary decorative cards.\r\n- Use reusable design tokens and shared components rather than styling each screen independently.\r\n\r\nThe finished product should look like a credible, premium event-tech startup, not a student dashboard template.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 3. REQUIRED TECH STACK\r\n\r\nUse the following stack unless the existing repository already has an equivalent working architecture:\r\n\r\n### Frontend\r\n\r\n- React\r\n- Vite\r\n- TypeScript\r\n- Tailwind CSS\r\n- shadcn/ui or similarly accessible reusable components\r"
    num_lines: 744
    num_bytes: 28548
    line_range_bytes: 4722
  }
}
