  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Evaluating Project Dependencies**\n\nI\'ve got the core dependencies, including `express`, `dotenv`, and `@google/genai`, all set up and ready. Packages like `tsx`, `lucide-react`, `motion`, `recharts`, and `@xyflow/react` are integrated. Now, I\'m thinking about setting the development and production scripts, considering `\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"` and `\"start\": \"node dist/server.js\"`.\n\n\n**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the API endpoints in `server.ts`. I\'m planning endpoints like `/api/quote/extract` for quotation extraction and `/api/ai/suggest-consequences` for downstream impact explanations.  I\'m also working on the data structures. The core type is `CelebrationEvent`, covering event specifics like event type, location, and budget. I\'m focusing on clean, modular design.\n\n\n**Refining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m deep in defining the data structures for the application. I\'ve fleshed out the `CelebrationEvent` with fields like venueCapacity, status, readinessScore, createdAt, and updatedAt. I am also working on `EventFunction`, `BudgetCategory`, `BudgetLineItem`, `ProvenanceRecord`, and `VendorQuote` which are now structured with their own specific properties. Each one is designed for detailed and comprehensive data management. I am considering the relationships between these structures.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve been working on expanding the existing data structures further. I\'ve designed `QuoteLineItem`, `PlanningTask`, `PriorityCompass`, `Scenario`, and `ScenarioChange`. These will be essential for managing quotes, planning tasks, defining priorities, and modeling different scenarios. I\'m focusing on their key properties and how they interrelate.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structures Further**\n\nI\'m now implementing `QuoteLineItem`, expanding on the data model with properties such as `originalAmount`, `revisedAmount`, and `rationale`. I am designing `RippleNode` for visualizing dependencies with properties such as `status` and `whyChanged`. I am also building `RippleSimulation`, incorporating properties like `activeScenario`, `guestCountDelta`, and `affectedNodeCount` to model potential impacts. I am considering ways to populate these with realistic data and scenarios.\n\n\n**Modeling Event Scenarios**\n\nI\'m now generating concrete, illustrative examples: a series of events like a Sangeet, Ceremony, and Reception, each with budgets, guest counts, and venue capacities. I\'ve broken down each event with categories like venue, catering, and decor, along with unit costs and provenance tags. I\'m focusing on illustrative budgets and starting scenarios, highlighting how changes in guest count trigger warnings related to venue capacity limits. I\'m modelling interconnected tasks with dependencies, and am looking at vendor quotations.\n\n\n**Developing Ripple Engine**\n\nI\'m now building the `rippleEngine` service. It will have pure, deterministic calculations. I\'m focusing on `calculateEventReadiness`, determining completion percentage, confirmed bookings, and budget variance. The `propagateRippleChanges` function is being fleshed out, including checking guest count changes, date shifts for milestones, and handling vendor quote hikes. I\'m planning to use illustrative scenarios, such as the need to confirm overtime charges and GST rates. I\'m also planning to create a demo, like a birthday bash.\n\n\n**Calculating Tradeoff Scenarios**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `calculateTradeoffScenarios` function. I am generating scenarios that involve precise mathematical calculations for cost reductions. These address budget overruns of \342\202\2713,00,000, with concrete scenarios. I am modeling specific changes, such as modifying decor, reducing food costs, and optimizing photography. The function returns the exact mathematics of each scenario, detailing itemized differences, remaining shortfalls or surpluses, and compromise notes. It will return a protected list. I\'m also preparing to build the `applyScenarioToEvent` function to directly update the active event state based on selected scenarios.\n\n\n**Generating iCalendar Exports**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `exportIcsCalendar(event)` function. This function creates a downloadable `.ics` iCalendar file, including all event functions and milestone details, for easy integration into calendars. I am incorporating provenance tags to show user inputs. I\'m also now thinking about adding the user_entered flag to the new iCalendar export.\n\n\n\n**Designing UI Mockups**\n\nI\'m now focusing on UI mockups. I\'m imagining a \"Simulate a Change\" spotlight drawer/modal, offering a multi-function timeline preview. I\'m also planning high-priority action items. I am envisioning a `BudgetStudio` with interactive category cards, line-item tables, and cost-per-guest analytics. I am planning a category breakdown chart using Recharts and a provenance inspector for data origin. I\'m also thinking about Add Category & Add Line Item modals. A React Flow interactive node network (`RippleEngine`) is planned, with scenario quick-trigger buttons and custom sliders for various adjustments.\n\n\n**Prioritizing UI Features**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on UI features, particularly the `TradeoffSimulatorModal`. I\'m planning a side-by-side comparison of scenarios, a confetti-triggering \"Apply Scenario\" button, and a new `VendorQuotes` section with upload and sample loaders. I\'m focusing on features to normalize vendor quotes, highlight missing data (\"Not mentioned \342\200\224 ask vendor\"), and generate multi-language inquiries. The `Timeline` component will have function tabs, task status toggles, an editor, a creator, and an iCalendar download. I am finalizing the `PrioritiesSettings` with drag/rank items and must-preserve locks. I am preparing alerts for missing data.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_553728"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import express, { Request, Response } from \'express\';\\nimport { createServer as createViteServer } from \'vite\';\\nimport path from \'path\';\\nimport dotenv from \'dotenv\';\\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \'@google/genai\';\\n\\ndotenv.config();\\n\\nconst app = express();\\nconst PORT = 3000;\\n\\napp.use(express.json({ limit: \'10mb\' }));\\napp.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: true, limit: \'10mb\' }));\\n\\n// Initialize Google Gen AI if key is present\\nconst apiKey = process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY;\\nlet genAI: GoogleGenAI | null = null;\\nif (apiKey && apiKey !== \'MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\') {\\n  genAI = new GoogleGenAI({ apiKey });\\n}\\n\\n// Health check endpoint\\napp.get(\'/api/health\', (req: Request, res: Response) => {\\n  res.json({\\n    status: \'ok\',\\n    aiEnabled: !!genAI,\\n    timestamp: new Date().toISOString()\\n  });\\n});\\n\\n// Quote extraction endpoint\\napp.post(\'/api/quote/extract\', async (req: Request, res: Response) => {\\n  try {\\n    const { rawText, fileBase64, mimeType, vendorNameHint } = req.body;\\n\\n    if (!genAI) {\\n      // Deterministic fallback response when Gemini key is not configured\\n      return res.json({\\n        success: true,\\n        source: \'deterministic_fallback\',\\n        warning: \'Demo mode active: Gemini API key not provided. Returning structured mock quote for demonstration.\',\\n        data: {\\n          vendorName: vendorNameHint || \'Royal Rasoi Grand Catering\',\\n          vendorCategory: \'Catering\',\\n          quoteDate: new Date().toISOString().split(\'T\')[0],\\n          validityPeriod: \'15 days from quote date\',\\n          totalAmount: 110000,\\n          subtotal: 100000,\\n          gstAmount: 5000,\\n          serviceCharges: 5000,\\n          paymentTerms: \'40% advance, 50% one day before event, 10% on completion\',\\n          cancellationPolicy: \'Non-refundable advance if cancelled within 14 days of event\',\\n          inclusions: [\\n            \'Live Chaat Counter (Pani Puri, Sev Puri, Aloo Tikki)\',\\n            \'Multi-course Gujarati & North Indian dinner menu\',\\n            \'4 Live Dessert counters including Jalebi-Rabdi\',\\n            \'Uniformed service staff (1 per 15 guests)\',\\n            \'Premium melamine dinnerware & copper chafing dishes\'\\n          ],\\n          exclusions: [\\n            \'Packaged mineral water bottles (billed on actual consumption)\',\\n            \'Liquor license and bar glassware\',\\n            \'Outdoor kitchen generator & fuel\'\\n          ],\\n          missingFields: [\\n            \'Per-hour overtime rate beyond 11:30 PM is not mentioned \342\200\224 ask vendor\',\\n            \'Staff gratuity / service tip expectation not specified \342\200\224 ask vendor\',\\n            \'Tasting session availability date not confirmed \342\200\224 ask vendor\'\\n          ],\\n          lineItems: [\\n            {\\n              id: \'qli-1\',\\n              description: \'Mehendi High-Tea Buffet (80 pax)\',\\n              quantity: 80,\\n              unitPrice: 350,\\n              subtotal: 28000\\n            },\\n            {\\n              id: \'qli-2\',\\n              description: \'Wedding & Sangeet Royal Feast (180 pax)\',\\n              quantity: 180,\\n              unitPrice: 400,\\n              subtotal: 72000\\n            }\\n          ]\\n        }\\n      });\\n    }\\n\\n    const systemInstruction = `You are Bandobast AI, an expert event quotation parser.\\nExtract structured vendor quotation details from the provided document or text.\\nAlways separate verified facts from missing details.\\nIf a field like overtime rate, GST percentage, or cancellation fee is not mentioned, DO NOT make up zero; instead, add it explicitly to \'missingFields\' with the note \\\"Not mentioned \342\200\224 ask vendor\\\".\\nReturn strictly valid JSON matching this schema:\\n{\\n  \\\"vendorName\\\": string,\\n  \\\"vendorCategory\\\": string,\\n  \\\"quoteDate\\\": string,\\n  \\\"validityPeriod\\\": string,\\n  \\\"totalAmount\\\": number,\\n  \\\"subtotal\\\": number,\\n  \\\"gstAmount\\\": number,\\n  \\\"serviceCharges\\\": number,\\n  \\\"paymentTerms\\\": string,\\n  \\\"cancellationPolicy\\\": string,\\n  \\\"inclusions\\\": string[],\\n  \\\"exclusions\\\": string[],\\n  \\\"missingFields\\\": string[],\\n  \\\"lineItems\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": string,\\n      \\\"description\\\": string,\\n      \\\"quantity\\\": number,\\n      \\\"unitPrice\\\": number,\\n      \\\"subtotal\\\": number\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}`;\\n\\n    const prompt = `Analyze this quotation and extract structured line items and terms:\\\\n${rawText || \'Refer to attached document\'}`;\\n\\n    let contents: any = prompt;\\n    if (fileBase64 && mimeType) {\\n      contents = [\\n        {\\n          inlineData: {\\n            data: fileBase64.replace(/^data:.*?;base64,/, \'\'),\\n            mimeType: mimeType\\n          }\\n        },\\n        prompt\\n      ];\\n    }\\n\\n    const response = await genAI.models.generateContent({\\n      model: \'gemini-2.5-flash\',\\n      contents: contents,\\n      config: {\\n        systemInstruction,\\n        responseMimeType: \'application/json\'\\n      }\\n    });\\n\\n    const parsedData = JSON.parse(response.text || \'{}\');\\n    return res.json({\\n      success: true,\\n      source: \'gemini_extracted\',\\n      data: parsedData\\n    });\\n  } catch (error: any) {\\n    console.error(\'Quote extraction error:\', error);\\n    return res.status(500).json({\\n      success: false,\\n      error: error.message || \'Failed to extract quotation\'\\n    });\\n  }\\n});\\n\\n// Vendor follow-up questions drafting endpoint\\napp.post(\'/api/quote/vendor-questions\', async (req: Request, res: Response) => {\\n  try {\\n    const { vendorName, category, missingFields, language = \'English\', context } = req.body;\\n\\n    if (!genAI) {\\n      // Deterministic templates for English, Hindi, and Gujarati\\n      let draft = \'\';\\n      if (language === \'Hindi\') {\\n        draft = `\340\244\250\340\244\256\340\244\270\340\245\215\340\244\244\340\245\207 ${vendorName},\\\\n\\\\n\340\244\271\340\244\256 \340\244\206\340\244\252\340\244\225\340\245\207 \340\244\255\340\245\207\340\244\234\340\245\207 \340\244\227\340\244\217 \340\244\225\340\245\213\340\244\237\340\245\207\340\244\266\340\244\250 \340\244\225\340\245\207 \340\244\262\340\244\277\340\244\217 \340\244\206\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\200 \340\244\271\340\245\210\340\244\202\340\245\244 \340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\207 \340\244\206\340\244\257\340\245\213\340\244\234\340\244\250 \340\244\225\340\245\207 \340\244\262\340\244\277\340\244\217 \340\244\225\340\245\201\340\244\233 \340\244\256\340\244\271\340\244\244\340\245\215\340\244\265\340\244\252\340\245\202\340\244\260\340\245\215\340\244\243 \340\244\265\340\244\277\340\244\265\340\244\260\340\244\243\340\245\213\340\244\202 \340\244\252\340\244\260 \340\244\270\340\245\215\340\244\252\340\244\267\340\245\215\340\244\237\340\245\200\340\244\225\340\244\260\340\244\243 \340\244\232\340\244\276\340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\217:\\\\n` +\\n          (missingFields || []).map((f: string, i: number) => `${i + 1}. ${f.replace(\' \342\200\224 ask vendor\', \'\')}`).join(\'\\\\n\') +\\n          `\\\\n\\\\n\340\244\225\340\245\203\340\244\252\340\244\257\340\244\276 \340\244\207\340\244\250 \340\244\254\340\244\277\340\244\202\340\244\246\340\245\201\340\244\223\340\244\202 \340\244\252\340\244\260 \340\244\234\340\244\262\340\245\215\340\244\246 \340\244\252\340\245\201\340\244\267\340\245\215\340\244\237\340\244\277 \340\244\225\340\244\260\340\245\207\340\244\202 \340\244\244\340\244\276\340\244\225\340\244\277 \340\244\271\340\244\256 \340\244\254\340\245\201\340\244\225\340\244\277\340\244\202\340\244\227 \340\244\225\340\245\213 \340\244\205\340\244\202\340\244\244\340\244\277\340\244\256 \340\244\260\340\245\202\340\244\252 \340\244\246\340\245\207 \340\244\270\340\244\225\340\245\207\340\244\202\340\245\244\\\\n\\\\n\340\244\270\340\244\270\340\245\215\340\244\250\340\245\207\340\244\271,\\\\n\340\244\206\340\244\257\340\245\213\340\244\234\340\244\225 \340\244\252\340\244\260\340\244\277\340\244\265\340\244\276\340\244\260 (\340\244\254\340\244\202\340\244\246\340\245\213\340\244\254\340\244\270\340\245\215\340\244\244)`;\\n      } else if (language === \'Gujarati\') {\\n        draft = `\340\252\250\340\252\256\340\252\270\340\253\215\340\252\244\340\253\207 ${vendorName},\\\\n\\\\n\340\252\244\340\252\256\340\252\276\340\252\260\340\252\276 \340\252\246\340\253\215\340\252\265\340\252\276\340\252\260\340\252\276 \340\252\256\340\253\213\340\252\225\340\252\262\340\252\276\340\252\265\340\253\207\340\252\262 \340\252\225\340\253\213\340\252\237\340\253\207\340\252\266\340\252\250 \340\252\254\340\252\246\340\252\262 \340\252\206\340\252\255\340\252\276\340\252\260. \340\252\205\340\252\256\340\252\276\340\252\260\340\252\276 \340\252\252\340\253\215\340\252\260\340\252\270\340\252\202\340\252\227\340\252\250\340\252\276 \340\252\206\340\252\257\340\253\213\340\252\234\340\252\250 \340\252\256\340\252\276\340\252\237\340\253\207 \340\252\250\340\253\200\340\252\232\340\253\207 \340\252\256\340\253\201\340\252\234\340\252\254\340\252\250\340\253\200 \340\252\254\340\252\276\340\252\254\340\252\244\340\253\213 \340\252\270\340\253\215\340\252\252\340\252\267\340\253\215\340\252\237 \340\252\225\340\252\260\340\252\265\340\252\276 \340\252\265\340\252\277\340\252\250\340\252\202\340\252\244\340\253\200:\\\\n` +\\n          (missingFields || []).map((f: string, i: number) => `${i + 1}. ${f.replace(\' \342\200\224 ask vendor\', \'\')}`).join(\'\\\\n\') +\\n          `\\\\n\\\\n\340\252\225\340\253\203\340\252\252\340\252\276 \340\252\225\340\252\260\340\253\200\340\252\250\340\253\207 \340\252\206 \340\252\265\340\252\277\340\252\227\340\252\244\340\253\213 \340\252\234\340\252\262\340\253\215\340\252\246\340\253\200 \340\252\252\340\253\201\340\252\267\340\253\215\340\252\237\340\252\277 \340\252\225\340\252\260\340\253\213 \340\252\234\340\253\207\340\252\245\340\253\200 \340\252\205\340\252\256\340\253\207 \340\252\250\340\252\277\340\252\260\340\253\215\340\252\243\340\252\257 \340\252\262\340\252\210 \340\252\266\340\252\225\340\253\200\340\252\217.\\\\n\\\\n\340\252\206\340\252\255\340\252\276\340\252\260,\\\\n\340\252\206\340\252\257\340\253\213\340\252\234\340\252\225 \340\252\252\340\252\260\340\252\277\340\252\265\340\252\276\340\252\260 (\340\252\254\340\252\202\340\252\246\340\253\213\340\252\254\340\252\270\340\253\215\340\252\244)`;\\n      } else {\\n        draft = `Dear ${vendorName} Team,\\\\n\\\\nThank you for providing the quotation for our celebration. Before we finalize the agreement, we would appreciate clarity on the following missing items:\\\\n\\\\n` +\\n          (missingFields || []).map((f: string, i: number) => `${i + 1}. ${f.replace(\' \342\200\224 ask vendor\', \'\')}`).join(\'\\\\n\') +\\n          `\\\\n\\\\nPlease let us know at your earliest convenience so we can proceed with securing the dates.\\\\n\\\\nWarm regards,\\\\nEvent Operations Coordinator (via Bandobast)`;\\n      }\\n\\n      return res.json({\\n        success: true,\\n        source: \'deterministic_template\',\\n        draft\\n      });\\n    }\\n\\n    const prompt = `You are a polite, firm event coordinator writing to ${vendorName} (${category}).\\nDraft a professional vendor clarification inquiry in ${language}.\\nAddress these specific ambiguities/omissions:\\n${(missingFields || []).join(\'\\\\n\')}\\nAdditional context: ${context || \'Multi-function family celebration\'}\\nKeep the tone warm, clear, and professional. Output ONLY the ready-to-send draft message.`;\\n\\n    const response = await genAI.models.generateContent({\\n      model: \'gemini-2.5-flash\',\\n      contents: prompt\\n    });\\n\\n    return res.json({\\n      success: true,\\n      source: \'gemini_generated\',\\n      draft: response.text?.trim()\\n    });\\n  } catch (error: any) {\\n    console.error(\'Follow-up draft error:\', error);\\n    return res.status(500).json({\\n      success: false,\\n      error: error.message || \'Failed to draft questions\'\\n    });\\n  }\\n});\\n\\n// Start server with Vite middleware in development\\nasync function startServer() {\\n  const isProd = process.env.NODE_ENV === \'production\';\\n\\n  if (!isProd) {\\n    const vite = await createViteServer({\\n      server: { middlewareMode: true },\\n      appType: \'spa\',\\n    });\\n    app.use(vite.middlewares);\\n  } else {\\n    // In production serve dist static assets\\n    app.use(express.static(path.resolve(__dirname, \'dist\')));\\n    app.get(\'*\', (req: Request, res: Response) => {\\n      res.sendFile(path.resolve(__dirname, \'dist\', \'index.html\'));\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  app.listen(PORT, \'0.0.0.0\', () => {\\n    console.log(`Bandobast Event Operations Server running at http://0.0.0.0:${PORT}`);\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nstartServer();\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create server.ts Express backend with Gemini API proxy and Vite middlewares\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/server.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing server.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create Express backend server\"}"
