  planner_response {
    response: "### Bandobast \342\200\224 Intelligent Event Operations Platform\n\n**Tagline:** *One change. A thousand connections. Bandobast keeps it together.*\n\nBuilt for **PromptWars Challenge 5: Celebration & Event Planner**, Bandobast is a celebration and event operations platform that connects budgets, vendor quotations, guest counts, family priorities, and deadlines into one living event twin.\n\nThe application functions both as a web application and an installable Progressive Web App (PWA) with desktop and mobile offline support.\n\n---\n\n### Key Built Capabilities & Workflow\n\n#### 1. Living Event Twin & Ripple Engine (The Signature Feature)\n- **Multi-Tier Dependency Graph:** Explicitly connects upstream drivers (Headcount & Auspicious Dates) $\\rightarrow$ direct dependents (Venue Capacity, Royal Rasoi Catering, Return Favors) $\\rightarrow$ downstream aggregators (Total Budget Ceiling & Task Deadlines).\n- **Preset 1 (Guest Increase 180 $\\rightarrow$ 220):** Recalculates per-guest catering plate costs, flags a high-contrast venue capacity overrun on Heritage Lawns (capacity: 200 pax; 20 over capacity), and adjusts gift order quantities.\n- **Preset 2 (Date Shift -14 Days Earlier):** Recomputes all date-dependent lead-times, flagging newly overdue milestones for family escalation.\n- **Preset 3 (Vendor Quote Hike +20%):** Models supplier price increases on catering and decor, recalculates the budget ceiling, and offers the trade-off simulator.\n- **Node Inspector:** Click any graph node to inspect causality, trigger source, authoritative data source, verification status, and recommended next actions.\n\n#### 2. Priority Compass & Trade-off Simulator\n- **Family Priority Ranking:** Rank and lock core non-negotiable priorities (*Food Quality*, *Guest Count*, *Photography*, *Decoration*, *Guest Experience*, *Convenience*).\n- **3 Genuinely Different Scenarios:**\n  1. **Protect the Feast:** Preserves live stations & 4-course banquet; trims decorative florals and drone package (saves \342\202\27126,000).\n  2. **Protect the Guest List:** Preserves full 220 guests; switches to digital cloud photo galleries and mobilizes contingency reserves (saves \342\202\27128,500).\n  3. **Protect the Memories:** Preserves 4K cinema teaser and heirloom album; re-purposes morning florals for evening stage and trims dessert redundancy (saves \342\202\27125,000).\n- **Apply to Living Plan:** Applies the approved scenario with celebratory confetti, updating category amounts, line items, and provenance across Budget Studio, Timeline, and the Living Twin.\n\n#### 3. Vendor Quote X-Ray & Clarification Drafter\n- **Quote Extraction:** Extracts deliverables, unit prices, subtotals, GST, and terms via the official Google Gen AI SDK (`@google/genai`), with deterministic fallback in demo mode.\n- **Omission Detection:** Explicitly flags unmentioned fees (*\"Overtime charges not mentioned \342\200\224 ask vendor\"*, *\"Staff gratuity not specified\"*).\n- **Multilingual Clarification Inquiries:** Drafts ready-to-send messages in **English**, **Hindi**, or **Gujarati** addressing specific quotation omissions.\n\n#### 4. Budget Studio with Data Provenance Audit\n- Categorized line items with dynamic `per_guest` and `fixed` pricing models.\n- Provenance tracking badges (`quoted`, `user_entered`, `ai_estimate`, `illustrative`) with modal audit trails explaining the calculation basis.\n- Live recalculation of totals, committed contracts, paid advances, remaining balance, and cost per guest.\n\n#### 5. Adaptive Timeline & Calendar Export\n- Function-filtered views (Mehendi, Sangeet, Vedic Wedding, Reception, and Combined Schedule).\n- Interactive milestone toggling updating overall **Event Readiness**.\n- Downloadable standard `.ics` iCalendar file for Google Calendar and Apple Calendar synchronization.\n\n#### 6. Multi-Event Versatility & PWA App Support\n- **Multi-Event Engine:** Supports Weddings, Milestone Birthdays, Engagements, Family Reunions, and Community Galas with preloaded sample events (*Aarav & Meera\'s Wedding* and *Arjun\'s 30th Birthday*).\n- **Installable PWA App:** Configured with `manifest.json`, Service Worker offline asset caching (`sw.js`), custom responsive icons, in-app install banner, and shortcut actions.\n\n---\n\n### Visual Design System\n- **Warm Ivory Background:** `#FAF7F0`\n- **White/Cream Card Surfaces:** `#FFFDF9`\n- **Forest Olive (Primary Accent):** `#405B43`\n- **Sage Green:** `#DCE6D6`\n- **Marigold (Celebration Highlights):** `#E7A83E`\n- **Terracotta (Secondary Accent):** `#C76F50`\n- **Espresso Text:** `#302F28`\n- **Typography:** Playfair Display for display headers + Plus Jakarta Sans for interface text.\n\n---\n\n### Verification & Testing\n- Automated test suite (`npm test`) passes all 8 test cases verifying deterministic budget arithmetic, ripple rules, venue capacity checks, date lead-time shifts, trade-off scenario generation, state application, and iCalendar generation.\n- Full TypeScript type-checking (`tsc --noEmit`) passes with 0 errors.\n- Full-stack Express backend with mounted Vite middlewares is running on port 3000 (`http://localhost:3000`)."
    modified_response: "### Bandobast \342\200\224 Intelligent Event Operations Platform\n\n**Tagline:** *One change. A thousand connections. Bandobast keeps it together.*\n\nBuilt for **PromptWars Challenge 5: Celebration & Event Planner**, Bandobast is a celebration and event operations platform that connects budgets, vendor quotations, guest counts, family priorities, and deadlines into one living event twin.\n\nThe application functions both as a web application and an installable Progressive Web App (PWA) with desktop and mobile offline support.\n\n---\n\n### Key Built Capabilities & Workflow\n\n#### 1. Living Event Twin & Ripple Engine (The Signature Feature)\n- **Multi-Tier Dependency Graph:** Explicitly connects upstream drivers (Headcount & Auspicious Dates) $\\rightarrow$ direct dependents (Venue Capacity, Royal Rasoi Catering, Return Favors) $\\rightarrow$ downstream aggregators (Total Budget Ceiling & Task Deadlines).\n- **Preset 1 (Guest Increase 180 $\\rightarrow$ 220):** Recalculates per-guest catering plate costs, flags a high-contrast venue capacity overrun on Heritage Lawns (capacity: 200 pax; 20 over capacity), and adjusts gift order quantities.\n- **Preset 2 (Date Shift -14 Days Earlier):** Recomputes all date-dependent lead-times, flagging newly overdue milestones for family escalation.\n- **Preset 3 (Vendor Quote Hike +20%):** Models supplier price increases on catering and decor, recalculates the budget ceiling, and offers the trade-off simulator.\n- **Node Inspector:** Click any graph node to inspect causality, trigger source, authoritative data source, verification status, and recommended next actions.\n\n#### 2. Priority Compass & Trade-off Simulator\n- **Family Priority Ranking:** Rank and lock core non-negotiable priorities (*Food Quality*, *Guest Count*, *Photography*, *Decoration*, *Guest Experience*, *Convenience*).\n- **3 Genuinely Different Scenarios:**\n  1. **Protect the Feast:** Preserves live stations & 4-course banquet; trims decorative florals and drone package (saves \342\202\27126,000).\n  2. **Protect the Guest List:** Preserves full 220 guests; switches to digital cloud photo galleries and mobilizes contingency reserves (saves \342\202\27128,500).\n  3. **Protect the Memories:** Preserves 4K cinema teaser and heirloom album; re-purposes morning florals for evening stage and trims dessert redundancy (saves \342\202\27125,000).\n- **Apply to Living Plan:** Applies the approved scenario with celebratory confetti, updating category amounts, line items, and provenance across Budget Studio, Timeline, and the Living Twin.\n\n#### 3. Vendor Quote X-Ray & Clarification Drafter\n- **Quote Extraction:** Extracts deliverables, unit prices, subtotals, GST, and terms via the official Google Gen AI SDK (`@google/genai`), with deterministic fallback in demo mode.\n- **Omission Detection:** Explicitly flags unmentioned fees (*\"Overtime charges not mentioned \342\200\224 ask vendor\"*, *\"Staff gratuity not specified\"*).\n- **Multilingual Clarification Inquiries:** Drafts ready-to-send messages in **English**, **Hindi**, or **Gujarati** addressing specific quotation omissions.\n\n#### 4. Budget Studio with Data Provenance Audit\n- Categorized line items with dynamic `per_guest` and `fixed` pricing models.\n- Provenance tracking badges (`quoted`, `user_entered`, `ai_estimate`, `illustrative`) with modal audit trails explaining the calculation basis.\n- Live recalculation of totals, committed contracts, paid advances, remaining balance, and cost per guest.\n\n#### 5. Adaptive Timeline & Calendar Export\n- Function-filtered views (Mehendi, Sangeet, Vedic Wedding, Reception, and Combined Schedule).\n- Interactive milestone toggling updating overall **Event Readiness**.\n- Downloadable standard `.ics` iCalendar file for Google Calendar and Apple Calendar synchronization.\n\n#### 6. Multi-Event Versatility & PWA App Support\n- **Multi-Event Engine:** Supports Weddings, Milestone Birthdays, Engagements, Family Reunions, and Community Galas with preloaded sample events (*Aarav & Meera\'s Wedding* and *Arjun\'s 30th Birthday*).\n- **Installable PWA App:** Configured with `manifest.json`, Service Worker offline asset caching (`sw.js`), custom responsive icons, in-app install banner, and shortcut actions.\n\n---\n\n### Visual Design System\n- **Warm Ivory Background:** `#FAF7F0`\n- **White/Cream Card Surfaces:** `#FFFDF9`\n- **Forest Olive (Primary Accent):** `#405B43`\n- **Sage Green:** `#DCE6D6`\n- **Marigold (Celebration Highlights):** `#E7A83E`\n- **Terracotta (Secondary Accent):** `#C76F50`\n- **Espresso Text:** `#302F28`\n- **Typography:** Playfair Display for display headers + Plus Jakarta Sans for interface text.\n\n---\n\n### Verification & Testing\n- Automated test suite (`npm test`) passes all 8 test cases verifying deterministic budget arithmetic, ripple rules, venue capacity checks, date lead-time shifts, trade-off scenario generation, state application, and iCalendar generation.\n- Full TypeScript type-checking (`tsc --noEmit`) passes with 0 errors.\n- Full-stack Express backend with mounted Vite middlewares is running on port 3000 (`http://localhost:3000`)."
