  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining ChatMessage Structure**\n\nI\'ve specified the foundational elements for managing chat message data within the `src/types/index.ts` file. I\'m adding a `ChatMessage` interface to structure each message. This interface will contain an `id`, a `role` (user, assistant, or system), and a `content` field that can accommodate both strings and code blocks.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now focusing on enriching the data models. I\'ve added a `ChatSession` interface to represent entire chat conversations, including an ID, title, event ID, budget, messages array, and timestamps. I\'m also adding a `VendorRecommendation` interface to encapsulate vendor details, encompassing various attributes like category, city, rating, estimated cost, and more. Lastly, I am adding navigation tabs, specifically \"home\" and \"chat\" to the `Sidebar.tsx`.\n\n\n**Adding AI Services**\n\nI\'m integrating AI functionalities now. I\'m adding `sendChatMessage` and `fetchBudgetVendorRecommendations` to `aiService.ts`. The second function will use structured JSON schemas with `gemini-3.8-flash` to return tailored vendor recommendations based on budget, event type, location, guest count, and category. I\'m also including `HomeHubView.tsx` with a new chat button and budget adjustor!\n\n\n**Designing AI Chat Interface**\n\nI\'m developing a dedicated AI chat interface in `AiChatView.tsx`. It will feature a header with the active session title, a \"New Chat\" button, a \"Saved Chats\" selector, and an inline budget adjuster. I plan to incorporate rich chat responses with formatted recommendations and quick actions, like applying the budget or adding vendors. Seamless prompt suggestions will also be included to guide users, such as \"Suggest best wedding venues in Jaipur under \342\202\2711,00,000\".\n\n\n"
